# November 23, 2026: Wichita, Kansas. Twelve old buildings in and near downtown Wichita, taken from the names in one
# walk-through video about the city's early buildings (the video is a tip only; nothing in these entries comes from it):
# the 1868 Munger house at Old Cowtown, the 1887 YMCA building that became the Scottish Rite Temple, the Eagles lodge,
# the Civil War monument by the old courthouse, the Carnegie library, the Catholic cathedral, Fiske Hall at Wichita
# State, the Garfield University building at Friends University, three hotels (Carey House/Eaton, Lassen, Broadview)
# and Union Station.
# Facts from the linked sources only: Wikipedia read one article at a time, the Kansas Historical Society's register
# search for Sedgwick County, and the owners' or managers' own pages.
